{"availability":"available","full":"loteran/Arctis-Sound-Manager","name":"Arctis-Sound-Manager","description":"SteelSeries headset manager for Linux — GG & Sonar alternative for Arctis: Sonar EQ with 330+ game presets, ChatMix, Game/Chat/Media mixer, spatial audio, sidetone, ANC, battery and OLED. Arctis Nova Pro Wireless & Wired, Nova Pro Omni, Nova Elite, Nova 7/7P/5/3, Arctis 7/7+/9/Pro Wireless, GameBuds. Built on PipeWire.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":154,"forks":17,"created":"2026-03-09T15:07:18Z","updated":"2026-10-06T16:51:50Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://loteran.github.io/Arctis-Sound-Manager/","topics":["arctis","arctis-nova-pro","arctis-nova-pro-wireless","bazzite","chatmix","equalizer","gaming-headset","headset","linux","linux-audio","linux-gaming","pipewire","sonar","spatial-audio","steam-deck","steelseries","steelseries-arctis","steelseries-gg","steelseries-sonar","wireless-headset"],"demo":"https://loteran.github.io/Arctis-Sound-Manager/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:42.762Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:42.762Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:42.762Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:42.762Z","stars":154,"forks":17}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The SteelSeries GG and Sonar alternative for Linux: manage your SteelSeries Arctis headset on Linux — device settings, 4-channel audio mixer (Game / Chat / Media / Output), automatic media routing, and a full Sonar EQ system powered by PipeWire filter-chain. New here? What works on Linux out of the box, and what ASM adds.","Supported Arctis headsets on Linux: Arctis Nova Pro Wireless, Arctis Nova Pro Wired, Arctis Nova Pro Omni, Arctis Nova Elite, Arctis Nova 7 (Gen 1 & Gen 2), Arctis Nova 7P, Arctis Nova 5 / 5X, Arctis Nova 3 / 3P / 3X, Arctis 7, Arctis 7+, Arctis 9 Wireless, Arctis Pro Wireless, Arctis 1 / 7X / 7P Wireless, and Arctis GameBuds / GameBuds X — full list with Product IDs in Supported devices.","🎚️ ASM Presets — browse and share community EQ presets! 🎨 ASM Themes — browse and share color themes, previewed on a miniature of the app! 💬 Join the Discord — chat, share presets and get help from the community! 📝 Share your experience in Discussions — feedback helps improve compatibility for everyone!"],"features":["4-channel mixer — separate Game, Chat, Media and Output virtual sinks","Automatic media routing — browsers and video players (Firefox, VLC, mpv…) are automatically routed to the Media sink","Smart stream adoption — apps running when ASM starts are pulled into ArctisMedia instead of staying on a non-Arctis sink","Manual stream control — move any audio stream between channels via G / C / M / O buttons; choices persist across restarts","Bring audio to headset — one click moves any app that got stuck on the wrong output (HDMI, S/PDIF, another sound card) back to your headset; available on the Home page and in the system tray"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/loteran/Arctis-Sound-Manager/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a9fe4cdda90ca3b92c036c33170b64638908de2f62491bae4009d13f744a9974","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:42.984Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:42.984Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The SteelSeries GG and Sonar alternative for Linux: manage your SteelSeries Arctis headset on Linux — device settings, 4-channel audio mixer (Game / Chat / Media / Output), automatic media routing, and a full Sonar EQ system powered by PipeWire filter-chain. New here? What works on Linux out of the box, and what ASM adds.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/loteran/Arctis-Sound-Manager/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"> The daemon (arctis-manager.service) starts automatically at login — the GUI is separate and must be opened manually the first time.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/loteran/Arctis-Sound-Manager/blob/main/README.md